n the extraction stage, we clone the\n            C source (coreutils, moreutils, grep, findutils) and analyze behavior directly from\n            the source of truth. In the specification stage, a human operator uses the make-work\n            and do-work Claude Code skills to produce two artifacts: a SRD (numbered requirements\n            and acceptance criteria covering all flags, exit codes, and stream behaviors) and a\n            use case (concrete end-to-end execution path through the system). Shared library\n            components (pkg/) also receive SRDs when their requirements span multiple utilities.\n            In the synthesis stage, the mage-claude-orchestrator library drives a Claude agent to\n            generate idiomatic Go from the SRD. In the verification stage, a differential testing\n--\n                agents for code generation. This is the boundary between the human-guided spec\n                phase and the automated synthesis phase.\n              capabilities:\n                - mage build compiles all binaries\n                - mage lint runs golangci-lint\n                - mage stats:loc prints LOC and doc word counts\n                - mage analyze runs cross-artifact consistency checks\n                - mage init initializes the project\n                - mage credentials extracts Claude credentials from macOS Keychain\n                - mage cobbler:measure and mage cobbler:stitch run the orchestrator generation cycle\n              references:\n                - magefiles/\n        design_decisions:\n            - id: 1\n              title: C source as the specification source of truth\n              decision: |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gyzds2pUBavWSveQydRHf7","session_id":"ba12ca9a-e35d-4fc7-aa12-3b09740d8dca","uuid":"d52143ea-d13e-4592-9bf4-c8bcf545967e","timestamp":"2026-05-19T21:26:53.601Z"}
