{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gyzds2pUBavWSveQydRHf7","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile my findings:\n\n## Task 5294 Summary\n\nBased on my analysis of the stitch prompt and SRD files, here is what task 5294 requires:\n\n### Task Description\nThe task is to **extend cmd/uniq to implement srd028 R3.1-R3.4** (Comparison options: -i, -f, -s, -w)\n\n### Requirements to Implement\n\nThe task focuses on implementing these four requirements from srd028-uniq.yaml:\n\n1. **R3.1 (-i flag)**: Case-insensitive comparison\n   - Lines that differ only in case are treated as duplicates\n   - Lines are compared case-insensitively but the original case is preserved in output\n\n2. **R3.2 (-f N flag)**: Skip first N fields (whitespace-separated tokens)\n   - Skips N whitespace-separated fields before comparing\n   - The skipped fields are still written to output\n   - Whitespace is treated as field separator (spaces and tabs)\n\n3. **R3.3 (-s N flag)**: Skip first N characters\n   - Skips N characters before comparing\n   - The skipped characters are still written to output\n\n4. **R3.4 (-w N flag)**: Compare only first N characters\n   - Compares only the first N characters of each line (after -f and -s adjustments)\n   - Characters beyond N are ignored for comparison but still written\n\n### Files to Modify\n- **cmd/uniq/main.go** - Extend the existing implementation\n- **cmd/uniq/uniq_test.go** - Add differential tests (tests are already present, just need code to pass them)\n\n### Current Status\nThe implementation in cmd/uniq/main.go **already supports all flags** (-i, -f, -s, -w):\n- Lines 18-26 define the options struct with all needed fields\n- Lines 76-143 implement parseFlags to handle all flags\n- Lines 187-211 implement comparisonKey function which applies all transformations\n- Lines 252-268 implement output formatting\n\nThe test file (uniq_test.go) **already contains comprehensive differential tests** for R3.1-R3.4:\n- Tests for R3.1 (-i): lines 270-310\n- Tests for R3.2 (-f): lines 312-352\n- Tests for R3.3 (-s): lines 354-376  \n- Tests for R3.4 (-w): lines 378-443\n- Combined flag tests included throughout\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- AC1-AC6: All SRD acceptance criteria must pass\n- AC5: Code must compile with `go build ./cmd/uniq/`\n- AC6: All tests must pass with `go test ./cmd/uniq/... -count=1`\n\nThe implementation appears to be complete and ready for testing against the guniq reference binary via the differential test framework."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ba12ca9a-e35d-4fc7-aa12-3b09740d8dca","uuid":"5f56c1ab-ed44-4ec7-b8a6-5382a33b2a4f","timestamp":"2026-05-19T21:27:14.880Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to find the stitch prompt for task 5294 in the go-unix-utils repo. Look at the most recent stitch prompt file in `.cobbler/history/` - specifically the file `2026-05-19-17-25-42-stitch-prompt.yaml` or the most recent stitch prompt. I need to find what requirements this task should implement and which files to create/modify. Search broadly - check the latest stitch-orchestrator.log and stitch-prompt.yaml files in .cobbler/history/.","agentId":"a990a80964f6556e3","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile my findings:\n\n## Task 5294 Summary\n\nBased on my analysis of the stitch prompt and SRD files, here is what task 5294 requires:\n\n### Task Description\nThe task is to **extend cmd/uniq to implement srd028 R3.1-R3.4** (Comparison options: -i, -f, -s, -w)\n\n### Requirements to Implement\n\nThe task focuses on implementing these four requirements from srd028-uniq.yaml:\n\n1. **R3.1 (-i flag)**: Case-insensitive comparison\n   - Lines that differ only in case are treated as duplicates\n   - Lines are compared case-insensitively but the original case is preserved in output\n\n2. **R3.2 (-f N flag)**: Skip first N fields (whitespace-separated tokens)\n   - Skips N whitespace-separated fields before comparing\n   - The skipped fields are still written to output\n   - Whitespace is treated as field separator (spaces and tabs)\n\n3. **R3.3 (-s N flag)**: Skip first N characters\n   - Skips N characters before comparing\n   - The skipped characters are still written to output\n\n4. **R3.4 (-w N flag)**: Compare only first N characters\n   - Compares only the first N characters of each line (after -f and -s adjustments)\n   - Characters beyond N are ignored for comparison but still written\n\n### Files to Modify\n- **cmd/uniq/main.go** - Extend the existing implementation\n- **cmd/uniq/uniq_test.go** - Add differential tests (tests are already present, just need code to pass them)\n\n### Current Status\nThe implementation in cmd/uniq/main.go **already supports all flags** (-i, -f, -s, -w):\n- Lines 18-26 define the options struct with all needed fields\n- Lines 76-143 implement parseFlags to handle all flags\n- Lines 187-211 implement comparisonKey function which applies all transformations\n- Lines 252-268 implement output formatting\n\nThe test file (uniq_test.go) **already contains comprehensive differential tests** for R3.1-R3.4:\n- Tests for R3.1 (-i): lines 270-310\n- Tests for R3.2 (-f): lines 312-352\n- Tests for R3.3 (-s): lines 354-376  \n- Tests for R3.4 (-w): lines 378-443\n- Combined flag tests included throughout\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- AC1-AC6: All SRD acceptance criteria must pass\n- AC5: Code must compile with `go build ./cmd/uniq/`\n- AC6: All tests must pass with `go test ./cmd/uniq/... -count=1`\n\nThe implementation appears to be complete and ready for testing against the guniq reference binary via the differential test framework."}],"totalDurationMs":70960,"totalTokens":49797,"totalToolUseCount":34,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":869,"cache_read_input_tokens":48236,"output_tokens":692,"ser