{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L6zVJDndeBiVgEkLTm9RgN","type":"tool_result","content":"8440\t    - Do NOT add features, refactoring, or improvements beyond what the requirements specify.\n8441\t    - Do NOT run any git commands. No git add, git commit, git init, git status, rm .git, or any other git operation. Git is managed externally by the orchestrator. Just write code and verify it compiles and passes tests.\n8442\t    - When building cmd/ binaries to verify compilation, use `go build -o bin/<name> ./cmd/<name>/` so outputs land in bin/ (which is git-ignored) rather than in the working directory.\n8443\t    - When a build or lint step fails, read ALL error and warning messages before making any changes. Fix every reported issue in a single edit pass, then run the build once to verify. Do not fix one issue, rebuild, fix the next — batch all fixes into one round.\n8444\t    - When modifying more than 3 locations in the same file, prefer the Write tool (full file replacement) over multiple Edit calls. Each Edit changes the file, invalidating old_string matches for subsequent Edits. Write avoids this by producing the complete file in one call.\n8445\t    - The test suite is the acceptance gate. Do not manually run binaries to compare output against reference implementations. Run `go test` and fix any failures. Manual comparison is only warranted when a test fails and the expected behavior is ambiguous.\n8446\t    - Complete all code changes before running `go build` or `go test`. Do not compile incrementally after each small edit. Mentally verify imports, types, and function signatures, then build once.\n8447\tdescription: |-\n8448\t    deliverable_type: code\n8449\t\n8450\t    required_reading:\n8451\t      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd028-uniq.yaml (full SRD, focus on R3.1-R3.4)\n8452\t      - cmd/uniq/main.go (existing implementation covering R1.1-R2.4)\n8453\t      - cmd/uniq/uniq_test.go (existing differential tests)\n8454\t      - pkg/testutils/ (RunDiffTests, BuildBinary, DiffTest pattern)\n8455\t\n8456\t    files:\n8457\t      - path: cmd/uniq/main.go\n8458\t        action: modify\n8459\t        note: Extend uniq implementation to cover srd028 R3.1-R3.4\n8460\t      - path: cmd/uniq/uniq_test.go\n8461\t        action: modify\n8462\t        note: Add differential tests for R3.1-R3.4\n8463\t\n8464\t    requirements:\n8465\t      - id: R1\n8466\t        text: \"Implement srd028 R3.1 per the SRD acceptance criteria\"\n8467\t      - id: R2\n8468\t        text: \"Implement srd028 R3.2 per the SRD acceptance criteria\"\n8469\t      - id: R3\n8470\t        text: \"Implement srd028 R3.3 per the SRD acceptance criteria\"\n8471\t      - id: R4\n8472\t        text: \"Implement srd028 R3.4 per the SRD acceptance criteria\"\n8473\t\n8474\t    design_decisions:\n8475\t      - id: D1\n8476\t        text: \"Follow the existing uniq implementation style in cmd/uniq/main.go -- extend, do not rewrite\"\n8477\t      - id: D2\n8478\t        text: \"Differential tests use testutils.RunDiffTests comparing against guniq from Homebrew coreutils\"\n8479\t      - id: D3\n8480\t        text: \"Reference binary lookup uses exec.LookPath(\\\"guniq\\\") with t.Skip if not found\"\n8481\t      - id: D4\n8482\t        text: \"All differential tests set LC_ALL=C in the Env field\"\n8483\t\n8484\t    acceptance_criteria:\n8485\t      - id: AC1\n8486\t        text: \"srd028 R3.1 acceptance criteria pass\"\n8487\t      - id: AC2\n8488\t        text: \"srd028 R3.2 acceptance criteria pass\"\n8489\t      - id: AC3\n8490\t        text: \"srd028 R3.3 acceptance criteria pass\"\n8491\t      - id: AC4\n8492\t        text: \"srd028 R3.4 acceptance criteria pass\"\n8493\t      - id: AC5\n8494\t        text: \"go build ./cmd/uniq/ compiles without errors\"\n8495\t      - id: AC6\n8496\t        text: \"go test ./cmd/uniq/... -count=1 passes (or skips if guniq not in PATH)\"\n8497\tshared_protocols:\n8498\t    - name: Differential testing\n8499\t      description: |\n8500\t        Every cmd/ package verifies its implementation by running the Go binary and the\n8501\t        Homebrew GNU reference binary side by side and comparing stdout, stderr, and exit\n8502\t        code via pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests. Test cases are defined as []testutils.DiffTest\n8503\t        slices in <utility>_test.go files. The harness sets LC_ALL=C by default.\n8504\t      pattern: |\n8505\t        func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n8506\t            goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n8507\t            refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"g<utility>\")\n8508\t            if err != nil { t.Skip(\"reference binary not found\") }\n8509\t            tests := []testutils.DiffTest{ ... }\n8510\t            testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n8511\t        }\n8512\t    - name: Graceful skip on missing reference binary\n8513\t      description: |\n8514\t        All cmd/ test files call exec.LookPath for the Homebrew reference binary at the\n8515\t        start of TestDiff and call t.Skip if it is not found. This allows the test suite\n8516\t        to run on machines without Homebrew GNU binaries installed without reporting false\n8517\t        failures. The binary is never installed by the test itself.\n8518\t      pattern: |\n8519\t        refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"g<utility>\")\n8520\t        if err != nil { t.Skipf(\"reference binary g<utility> not in PATH: %v\", err) }\n8521\t    - name: SIGPIPE handling\n8522\t      description: |\n8523\t        All cmd/ utilities that write to stdout call pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at\n8524\t        the start of main. This ensures the process exits 0 when piped output is consumed\n8525\t        by a downstream consumer that closes its stdin (e.g., head, grep -q), matching GNU\n8526\t        coreutils behavior.\n8527\t      pattern: |\n8528\t        func main() {\n8529\t            sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n8530\t            ...\n8531\t        